MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Minyi,
Can't recommend pi charts much, but you don't have many levels so it's not so bad.

As far as I know, you can't have two colors within a single string using geom_text, but you can get close to what you want by splitting the labels into two separate text commands. It's a bit "hacky", but it does work if you align them both the same and insert a newline character before the second character. I found that with only one newline it overlaps, but with two it looks close to what you have already.

library(tidyverse) #don't need cowplot for this

c_title<-data.frame(titles=c("Prof", "Asso Prof","Lecture","Primary"),
                        nums=c(20,25,10,5))

c_title <-
c_title %>%
mutate(
titles = factor(titles, levels = c("Primary","Lecture", "Asso Prof","Prof")), # make this an ordered factor
Percentage = sprintf("%.1f",c_title$nums/sum(c_title$nums)*100), # calculate percentage
pie_text = paste("\n\n", Percentage,"%", sep=""), # newlinex2 + percentage% label
num_p = paste(nums, pie_text, sep="\n") # not really necessary anymore

)
#plot
ggplot(data = c_title, aes(x = "", y = nums, fill = titles)) +
geom_bar(stat = "identity",width = 1) +

geom_text(aes(label = nums), position = position_stack(vjust = 0.5),color="red") + # use nums as first label without newline
geom_text(aes(label = pie_text), position = position_stack(vjust = 0.5), color = "black")+ #use pie_text as secondary label with newlines

coord_polar(theta = "y",direction = -1)+
labs(x ="", y = "", title = "") +  #
theme(axis.line = element_blank())+ #remove the axis
theme(axis.ticks =  element_blank(),axis.text = element_blank(),
           legend.position=c(0.2,0),legend.justification=c(0,1)) +#remove the -
guides(fill=guide_legend(title = NULL,nrow=1)) #remove title of legend

HTH,
B

